# `!`-move of a collection with a LIVE element borrow, move-REASSIGN shape
# (`w = !v` into an existing slot). Same class as the move-BIND fixture:
# the element borrow must be materialized at the move site or the
# post-move mutation reads through ("gamma" instead of "alpha").
# Bind shape MUST be `.get(i).unwrap()` — `v[i]` is already-safe.
void main():
    Vector[String] v = ["alpha", "beta"]
    String first = v.get(0).unwrap()
    Vector[String] w = ["zeta"]
    w = !v
    w.set(0, "gamma")
    print(first)
    print(w.get(0).unwrap())
